{"name":"Piercing Pink","hex":"#dd00ee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"piercing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of pierce"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["gerund of pierce","A hole made in the body so that jewellery can be worn through it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piercing"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Body piercing","blocks":[{"text":"Body piercing is a form of body modification involving the puncturing or cutting a part of the body to create an opening through which jewelry or implants can be worn or inserted. The word piercing can refer to the act or practice of body piercing, or to an opening in the body created by this act or practice. It can also, by metonymy, refer to the resulting decoration, or to the decorative jewelry used. Piercing implants alter the body and/or skin profile and appearance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Body_art.jpg/330px-Body_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_piercing","wikidata":"Q157943"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"htt